---
import './freshness.css';
---
<figure class="fresh-figure">
 <div class="figure-heading"><span class="figure-number">Figure 5</span>Choose a revision before choosing its cached card</div>
 <div class="scene">
  <ol class="timeline">
   <li><strong>Read the authoritative source revision.</strong> It returns 2 for north’s P7.</li>
   <li><strong>Look up the revision 2 card.</strong> The old revision 1 card is under a different key.</li>
   <li><strong>On a miss, obtain matching source data.</strong> Read revision and product together. If the revision has changed, select the new revision instead.</li>
   <li><strong>Build and save under that data’s revision.</strong> Check the cached payload matches its key before returning it.</li>
  </ol>
  <div class="row">
   <div class="box"><p class="label">Old key · not selected</p><code>product:v1:north:P7:en-GB:GBP:r1</code><span>GBP 20.00 · revision 1</span></div>
   <div class="box changed"><p class="label">Selected key</p><code>product:v1:north:P7:en-GB:GBP:r2</code><span>GBP 22.00 · revision 2</span></div>
  </div>
  <p class="callout">A delayed revision 1 fill can only populate the r1 key. A reader that selected revision 2 never looks there.</p>
 </div>
 <figcaption>The representation version <code>v1</code> stays fixed; <code>r1</code> and <code>r2</code> identify source revisions. Every relevant source change must advance the revision, and a revision must never be reused for different data.</figcaption>
</figure>
